# .civicignore — paths excluded from the Dependency Delta scanner.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments.  Blank lines are ignored.
# Each non-comment line is a repository-relative glob pattern (matched
# with fnmatch.fnmatch, case-sensitive) applied against changed file
# paths.  Matching files are silently skipped — no scan command is
# generated and no error is raised.
#
# Use cases:
#   - Projects that require local-only tooling not available on CI
#     (e.g. CS2 Modding Toolkit for CivicSurvival.csproj)
#   - Generated lock files that are verified by a different gate
#   - Documentation-only changes that happen to touch a manifest dir

# CS2 Modding Toolkit projects — dotnet restore requires Mod.props
# from a local CS2 installation that is unavailable on CI runners.
CivicSurvival/CivicSurvival.csproj
